<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ngo Quyen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">897–944</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ngo Quyen was a Vietnamese general who defeated a fleet of the Southern Han at the Battle of Bach Dang in 938, luring its ships onto iron-tipped stakes planted in the river bed. The victory ended about a thousand years of Chinese rule over northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. He proclaimed himself king in 939 and founded the short-lived Ngo dynasty at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/co-loa-citadel">Co Loa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ngo-quyen.jpg" alt="Ngo Quyen" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bùi Thụy Đào Nguyên · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:T%C6%B0%E1%BB%A3ng_Ng%C3%B4_Quy%E1%BB%81n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
